  "notes": "The drummer-turned-producer-turned-label-head, and the entry says the groove is always the point. Two drum facts drive this model. The pattern: \"hard 2&4, quarter-note kick under choruses (four-on-the-floor-adjacent), 8th hats, crash accents on chorus downbeats, and **fills placed only at 4- and 8-bar boundaries**. Low ornament, high consistency, pocket prioritised over flash.\" The lineage: \"he came out of Texas/Louisiana R&B session drumming (his own biggest early production credit is a multi-million-selling soul record), which shows up as a heavier, more soul-derived backbeat than the Nashville norm\" — a soul backbeat is a ghosted, slightly-behind one, so the ghost probability runs high and the snare carries a small positive offset, which is what separates this model from the arena-country producers who share its tempo band. Harmony is \"I–IV–V and I–♭VII–IV with two-chord I–V anthem vamps,\" so the two-chord family and a `vamp` weight are authored. The bass is \"locked to the kick on 1 and 3, 8ths under choruses, kept low and simple so the guitars own the mids,\" hence `mirror_kick` with a low register ceiling. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high) — \"the drumming lineage and chart record are documented; per-session gear is not [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the offset value, the velocity tiers and the counter ratio.",
